            "content": "# WebSocket Persistent Subscription Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Add three MCP tools (`startSubscription`, `readMessages`, `stopSubscription`) that let an AI maintain persistent WebSocket connections to Bybit streams and poll accumulated messages on demand.\n\n**Architecture:** A singleton `SubscriptionManager` holds a `Map<id, Subscription>` of live WebSocket connections. Each subscription buffers incoming messages (capped at 500), reconnects transparently on drops (up to 3 times with exponential backoff), and auto-expires after 5 minutes of no `readMessages` calls. Three hand-written tools (outside the code-generator pipeline) expose create/read/stop operations. They are registered in `server.ts` alongside the auto-generated tools.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Node.js `ws` (already in deps), TypeScript, `crypto.randomUUID()` for IDs, existing `resolveSignConfig` / `signHmac` / `signRsa` for WS auth, `zod` for input validation.\n\n---\n\n## File Map\n\n| Action | Path | Responsibility |\n|--------|------|----------------|\n| Create | `src/client/subscription-manager.ts` | SubscriptionManager class + singleton export |\n| Create | `src/tools/subscription/startSubscription.ts` | MCP tool: open a new subscription |\n| Create | `src/tools/subscription/readMessages.ts` | MCP tool: read buffered messages |\n| Create | `src/tools/subscription/stopSubscription.ts` | MCP tool: close a subscription |\n| Create | `src/tools/subscription/index.ts` | Export `subscriptionTools` array |\n| Modify | `src/server.ts` | Import and merge `subscriptionTools` into `allTools` |\n\n---\n\n## Task 1: SubscriptionManager core\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `src/client/subscription-manager.ts`\n\n### 内部数据结构\n\n```typescript\ninterface Subscription {\n  id: string;\n  ws: WebSocket;\n  topic: string;\n  category: WsCategory;\n  requiresAuth: boolean;\n  messages: unknown[];\n  readonly maxMessages: number;   // default 500\n  lastReadAt: number;             // ms timestamp\n  createdAt: number;\n  status: 'connecting' | 'active' | 'reconnecting' | 'closed';\n  reconnectAttempts: number;\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Create `src/client/subscription-manager.ts` with skeleton**\n\n```typescript\nimport WebSocket from 'ws';\nimport crypto from 'crypto';\nimport { resolveSignConfig, signHmac, signRsa } from '../utils/auth.js';\nimport { commonHeaders } from '../version.js';\nimport type { WsCategory } from './ws-client.js';\n\nconst WS_MAINNET: Record<WsCategory, string> = {\n  linear:  'wss://stream.bybit.com/v5/public/linear',\n  spot:    'wss://stream.bybit.com/v5/public/spot',\n  inverse: 'wss://stream.bybit.com/v5/public/inverse',\n  option:  'wss://stream.bybit.com/v5/public/option',\n  private: 'wss://stream.bybit.com/v5/private',\n  spread:  'wss://stream.bybit.com/v5/public/spread',\n  misc:    'wss://stream.bybit.com/v5/public/misc/status',\n};\n\nconst WS_TESTNET: Record<WsCategory, string> = {\n  linear:  'wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/public/linear',\n  spot:    'wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/public/spot',\n  inverse: 'wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/public/inverse',\n  option:  'wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/public/option',\n  private: 'wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/private',\n  spread:  'wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/public/spread',\n  misc:    'wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/public/misc/status',\n};\n\nconst MAX_MESSAGES = 500;\nconst IDLE_EXPIRE_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000;   // 5 minutes\nconst MAX_RECONNECT_ATTEMPTS = 3;\nconst RECONNECT_BASE_MS = 1000;\n\ninterface Subscription {\n  id: string;\n  ws: WebSocket;\n  topic: string;\n  category: WsCategory;\n  requiresAuth: boolean;\n  messages: unknown[];\n  maxMessages: number;\n  lastReadAt: number;\n  createdAt: number;\n  status: 'connecting' | 'active' | 'reconnecting' | 'closed';\n  reconnectAttempts: number;\n}\n\nexport interface StartOptions {\n  category: WsCategory;\n  topic: string;\n  requiresAuth?: boolean;\n  maxMessages?: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ReadResult {\n  subscriptionId: string;\n  status: Subscription['status'];\n  messageCount: number;\n  messages: unknown[];\n}\n\nexport class SubscriptionManager {\n  private subs = new Map<string, Subscription>();\n  private timer: ReturnType<typeof setInterval>;\n\n  constructor() {\n    // Auto-expire idle subscriptions every 60 seconds.\n    this.timer = setInterval(() => this.expireIdle(), 60_000);\n    // Allow process to exit even if timer is active.\n    if (typeof this.timer.unref === 'function') this.timer.unref();\n  }\n\n  // ── public API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  start(opts: StartOptions): string { throw new Error('not implemented'); }\n  read(id: string, limit?: number, clearAfterRead?: boolean): ReadResult { throw new Error('not implemented'); }\n  stop(id: string): void { throw new Error('not implemented'); }\n  list(): Array<{ id: string; topic: string; status: string; buffered: number }> { throw new Error('not implemented'); }\n\n  // ── internals ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  private expireIdle(): void { /* TODO */ }\n  private openWebSocket(sub: Subscription): void { /* TODO */ }\n  private authenticate(ws: WebSocket, topic: string, onAuth: () => void, onFail: (e: Error) => void): void { /* TODO */ }\n}\n\nexport const subscriptionManager = new SubscriptionManager();\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Implement `openWebSocket` — connect, auth if needed, subscribe, collect messages**\n\nReplace the `openWebSocket` stub:\n\n```typescript\nprivate openWebSocket(sub: Subscription): void {\n  const urls = process.env.BYBIT_TESTNET === 'true' ? WS_TESTNET : WS_MAINNET;\n  const ws = new WebSocket(urls[sub.category], { headers: commonHeaders() });\n  sub.ws = ws;\n  sub.sta